LOCAL PATCH — Caravel, 2026-09-25 (not upstream; the source repo is not on this machine)
======================================================================================
The writer had no seam for its fee input. It found private outputs with its own module-private
scanUtxos: ONE request for the 1000 OLDEST rows of ONE indexer's /utxos. Once the network passed
1000 unspent outputs, a wallet whose private coins were all recent saw none and CNS reported
"No confidential UTXOs found — this wallet needs a balance to pay the fee" with ~2000 tTARI
private. The fee input also never reached Caravel's spend record.

Two optional BrowserSigner fields, both no-ops when absent (the writer then behaves exactly as
at ed6ca72):

  ownedUtxos?: () => Promise<OwnedFeeUtxo[]>
      browser-writer.js buildSubmit: used INSTEAD of scanUtxos. Caravel passes its own
      scanOwnedUtxos (paginated, both indexers, by-id recovery, receive scan, spend-record
      exclusion). The objects are the same shape scanUtxos already produced.

  onSubmitted?: (txId, spentInputIds) => void
      browser-writer.js buildSubmit: called after submitTransaction on a REAL submit (never on a
      dry-run), before pollResult. Caravel locks the fee input in its spend record here.

Selection, fee math, the dry-run budget and every message are unchanged. The .js.map files were
not regenerated. Upstream the same two fields to ootle-name-service before the next re-vendor, or
re-apply this patch on top of it.
